'use strict';

/**
 * Every Modbus register the Huawei specification defines, per device.
 *
 * This is a reference list, not a polling list. lib/modbus-registers.js holds the registers
 * the app actually reads and writes, roughly ninety of them; this file holds all the ones
 * the document describes, so the Registers tab can answer "what else is in there" rather
 * than only showing what we happen to use.
 *
 * Source: SUN2000MA V100R001C00SPC177 Modbus Interface Definitions, section 3
 *   3.1 Inverter Equipment Register  -> inverter
 *   3.2 Battery Equipment Register   -> battery
 *   3.3 Meter Equipment Register     -> meter
 *
 * The EMMA drivers, the SDongle and the smart charger are documented elsewhere and are not
 * in here; their Registers tab keeps showing the app's own list alone.
 *
 * Fields per row:
 *   address       the Modbus register address
 *   length        how many 16-bit words it occupies (the spec's Quantity column)
 *   type          the decoder in lib/modbus-client.js, or null where the spec's type is not
 *                 a scalar this app can decode (MLD/Bytes, MULTIDATA and the like). A null
 *                 type means the row is listed but cannot be read into a value.
 *   specType      the type exactly as the spec writes it, so the list stays checkable
 *   label         the signal name as the spec writes it
 *   unit          the spec's unit, blank where it says N/A
 *   decimalPower  -log10(Gain): what the raw value must be scaled by to land in `unit`
 *   rw            RO, RW or WO
 *   conflict      present only where the specification contradicts itself about this
 *                 register, which today means a type that needs more words than the
 *                 Quantity column gives it. Such a row is listed but has no `type`, so
 *                 nothing offers a read that could only fail.
 *
 * Generated rather than typed, and checked against the specification's own tables: every
 * row of the inverter section agrees on name, type, unit, gain, quantity and read/write.
 * See test/modbus-spec-registers.test.js.
 */

